				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200783" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;" >TheMightyMcB</a></span> <span class="odate time_1556760635 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 May 2019 01:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4235809">
									

<p>Before I get into my little review here, I should mention that you haven't hosted your image on-site. You should probably do that (it's under the &quot;Files&quot; option at the bottom of the page). Just change the file name in the image block to be what the image is called.</p>
<p>Anyways, let's get to it!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>2m2 area of SCP-4281</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Assuming you mean that to be &quot;2m<sup>2</sup> area around SCP-4281&quot;, yeah? Superscripts are made by bookending whatever is getting sent up with &quot;^^&quot;, so you'd type in &quot;<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">^^2^^</span>&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Anyone hearing these exclamations will be overwhelmed with a feeling of intense embarrassment.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not gonna lie, this kind of feels like a cop out. I don't know what else you could do, but &quot;intense embarrassment&quot; feels cheap.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>sound-blocking technology or possessing a hearing impediment</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like neither of those are the correct technical terms for what they describe. &quot;soundproofing/noise-cancelling&quot; and &quot;hearing impairment&quot; are probably what you're looking for.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Individuals who manage to look inside SCP-4281-1's stall are wholly incapable of describing the interior.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Continuing to feel like a cop-out. How did they look inside if all of the above was true? I would pick one deterrent and stick with it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>phrases such as “That’s right, huh? Of course it is.”, “Another thing about that…”, “And, heck, you know what that reminds me of?”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing your &quot;and&quot; to separate the three features of the list. Might wanna start the last quote with &quot;Heck&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the Foundation, and several GOI's</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be &quot;the Foundation and several GOIs.&quot; or &quot;the Foundation, as well as several GOIs.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Clarke remained in the stall for an additional 3 hours, fruitlessly attempting to guide the conversation back to topics of interest.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This whole log was fucking amazing, and I loved every minute of it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Test Log - 4281-1-01</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Test 05 is titled as Test 01.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Test Log - SCP-4281-1-05</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one wasn't as funny as the first one, but I can't see a version of this that doesn't dash your pacing to the rocks without including it. Maybe trim it down slightly?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Test Log - SCP-4281-1-13</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay woah, I did not see this coming, and holy shit was it good. I would honestly have upvoted if this was just the first log, not gonna lie. Some crazy cowboy in a bathroom stall that doesn't shut up. But then this hit, and goddamn.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4281-1: God dang it. Things were going so well. What'd I do wrong? People like talkin' about themselves, right? … I shoulda' just told him the trucker story. Everyone loves that story. Or maybe I shoulda' mentioned-… nah, he would have found that boring. Maybe I coulda'- no, that's just stupid. Dang it. Dang it!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>With my previous compliment, I do have a caveat. I'm not a fan of this as the ending. The whole way through that interview, I was thinking that -1 was getting all personal and nasty due to their attempt at being fake to him (lying, etc.), and then this final bit here clashes with that change in temper in a way that I'm not sure I like. I honestly think it'd be better if you ended at &quot;So I said to him- Oh! Uh, well, alright then! Have a good night fellas! Come back any time!&quot;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, this was totally unexpected and honestly really good. I enjoyed myself, and the dialogue was excellent. Take that +1, man. Good stuff.</p>

							</div>

								
					
