			<div class="content" id="post-content-4238761">
									

<p>Thank you!</p>
<p>I had considered Euclid, but honestly, the Foundation can only base their containment procedures on what they currently know. Any number of safe-level SCPs could, by virtue of just being &quot;anomalous&quot;, be Euclid, but thus far have proven easy to contain.</p>
<p>Yes, SCP-4281-1 is mysterious, and knows a great deal, but as far as the Foundation has seen, it's stationary, and they can easily control who has access to that knowledge with a few guards and a locked door.</p>

