<p>I think my only serious complaints are that the DATA EXPUNGED should (probably) be DATA REDACTED (expunged means no one is allowed to see it), and that the central anomaly preventing interaction/perception with him is a little too ornate (drones failing, compulsion effects, etc). I feel there's probably a simple, more elegant way to prevent interaction that doesn't rely on these effects.</p>
<p>The interviews are fun, and have a weird charm. This reminds me a lot of <a href="/scp-270">SCP-270</a>, actually (a phone that gives just enough sensitive information to keep the Foundation listening), except now the voice has a personality and more character. The final bit is what got me to upvote, since it manages to subvert the expectation of sinister motivations (which you set up with the whole Lawrence thing).</p>

